# __PROJECT_TITLE__ — project memory

This folder is the **project tier** of the team's AI-agent memory: everything an agent needs to
know about `__PROJECT_NAME__` that is *not* a company-wide fact. Company-wide facts (who we are,
vendors, roles, company conventions, cross-project ADRs) live in **cairn** (Basic Memory
project `cairn`). Both are Markdown, both are indexed by Basic Memory, both sync through git.

Created __DATE__ from `cairn/templates/project-memory`.

## Layout

| Folder | Holds | Agents may |
|---|---|---|
| `context/` | overview, architecture, conventions, glossary of THIS project | propose only |
| `decisions/` | project-scoped ADRs | propose only |
| `log/` | gotchas, learnings, `PROPOSAL - …` notes | write freely |
| `scripts/` | `sync-memory.{sh,ps1,py}` — pull before, commit+push after (hooks) | — |

## Trust order
`decisions/` (accepted) > `context/` > `log/` inside this tier. Across tiers, **scope wins**: a
project fact here beats a stale mention in cairn; a company fact in cairn beats a
project note that contradicts it. Contradiction → flag to the human, never pick silently.

## Rules
The six agent rules are in `AGENT-RULES.md` (imported by the repo's `CLAUDE.md`, mirrored in
`.cursor/rules/memory.mdc` and `.kiro/steering/memory.md`). The step-by-step loop is the
`team-memory` skill.

